{
  "dom_id": "step-e3635",
  "name": "Example: Differentiating a Product Containing an Exponential or Logarithmic Function",
  "problem": "Given that $f(x)=x^2\\ln x,$ find $f'(x).$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = x^2$ and $v(x)=\\ln x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{\u2032}ln\u2061x+{x}^{2}{(ln\u2061x)}^{\u2032} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot ln\u2061x+{x}^{2}(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =2xln\u2061x+x \\\\  & =x(2ln\u2061x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
